assessment":"The exact Mishnah and Rashi preserve the statement, and Rashi explicitly identifies Chalafta as the father’s name.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bekhorot 26a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot_26a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Bekhorot 26a:3:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot_26a.3.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1323:1:citation-08","he":[302,412],"en":[586,614],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_70a.16"},"reference":"Bava Kamma 70a:16","assessment":"Both Bavli passages keep both directions. The end of the entry argues from one alternative, not an established exclusive transmission.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Kamma 70a:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_70a.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 56b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_56b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1323:1:citation-09","he":[302,412],"en":[616,630],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_56b.3"},"reference":"Bava Batra 56b:3","assessment":"Both Bavli passages keep both directions. The end of the entry argues from one alternative, not an established exclusive transmission.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Kamma 70a:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_70a.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 56b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_56b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1323:1:citation-10","he":[628,757],"en":[1010,1022],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_105b.8"},"reference":"Shabbat 105b:8","assessment":"The exact Shabbat has Chilfa bar Agra transmitting Yochanan ben Nuri. The checked Rif has Chalafta ben Agra, attributes the introduction to R. Shimon and ends with R. Yochanan alone.",