:"ואלעזר בן מתיא וחנניה בן חכינאי","reason":"Sotah names Eliezer ben Matya and the received text has Elazar. Preserve the difference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 34a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_34a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ר' חלפתא (וכן הוא גירסת האלפסי וגי' שלפנינו חילפא) בר אגרא","reason":"The checked Rif also differs in ben Agra, omits Shimon’s patronymic, and has bare Rabbi Yochanan. Preserve the precise report in the root and the alternative learning directions.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rif Shabbat 38a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Shabbat_38a.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Shabbat 105b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_105b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Kamma 70a:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_70a.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 56b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_56b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ואולי ר' יהודה בר אגרא אחיו (ע\"ש)","reason":"The reciprocal notice gives a possible brother. Identity remains unresolved.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 207:1","target":{"entry":207,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The two Gamliels, Tzippori practice, quotations and competing learning directions have exact witnesses. Yuchasin supplies the Shimon inference. The Jordan roster and Rif wordings retain their variants.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Taanit 2:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Taanit_2.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Bekhorot 26a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot_26a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Bekhorot 26a:3:1","target":{"url":"https://w